# no-silent-truncation.sh watchlist — one substring per line, matched against the raw
# Bash command text. Any command CONTAINING one of these lines as a substring is treated
# as "a search over protected data," and piping it through head/tail/sed -n/--limit gets
# blocked (see the hook's own comments for why).
#
# install.sh copies this file to .claude/hooks/no-silent-truncation.watchlist in the
# target repo and stops there — it does NOT try to guess your tools. Edit the installed
# copy to name the things that actually search your protected data: a mail indexer, a
# notes search, a call log, a transcript search, grep over specific data directories,
# whatever exists in this repo. Lines starting with # are comments; blank lines ignored.
#
# Starter examples (uncomment/adapt, or delete and write your own):
# mailq
# notesq
# shotq
# imsgq
# callq
# recall
# convoq
